WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:17.097
Unit fifteen: B2 First: Listening and Speaking. Today you will listen for opinion and attitude and speak with a partner.

4
00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:19.875
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.834
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:25.603
Opinion.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:28.779
Opinion means what someone thinks.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:30.802
Listen for opinion.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.243
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:37.927
Opinion.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:39.719
Attitude.

12
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:43.018
Attitude means how someone feels.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:44.966
What is his attitude?

14
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.017
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

15
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:51.961
Attitude.

16
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:53.671
Purpose.

17
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:56.799
Purpose means the reason for speaking.

18
00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:59.058
Identify the purpose.

19
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.105
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

20
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:05.921
Purpose.

21
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:07.708
Extract.

22
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.716
Extract means a short recording.

23
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.736
Listen to the extract.

24
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.979
Your turn. Say: Extract.

25
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:19.707
Extract.

26
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.451
Collaborate.

27
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.380
Collaborate means to work together.

28
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.635
Collaborate with your partner.

29
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.902
Your turn. Say: Collaborate.

30
00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:33.803
Collaborate.

31
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:35.563
Justify.

32
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.014
Justify means to give reasons for a view.

33
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:41.140
Justify your choice.

34
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.426
Your turn. Say: Justify.

35
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.465
Justify.

36
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:50.102
Compare.

37
00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:53.941
Compare means to say how things are similar or different.

38
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.050
Compare the two photos.

39
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.035
Your turn. Say: Compare.

40
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.889
Compare.

41
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.732
Interact.

42
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:08.448
Interact means to speak with another person.

43
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.550
Interact naturally.

44
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.686
Your turn. Say: Interact.

45
00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:17.581
Interact.

46
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.134
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:25.947
Visal, what is tested in B2 First Listening?

48
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:42.032
There are four parts: short extracts, a monologue with sentence completion, a conversation with multiple matching and a longer interview. You listen for opinion, attitude and purpose.

49
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:44.965
How can I listen for attitude?

50
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:55.541
Listen to words and tone. Words like unfortunately or frankly can show feelings, and the tone may show if the speaker is pleased or worried.

51
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.499
What about the Speaking test?

52
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:14.008
You speak with a partner in four parts: personal questions, comparing two photos, a collaborative task and a discussion. Give reasons, ask your partner questions and respond to their ideas.

53
00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:16.644
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.483 --> 00:03:22.107
Grammar focus: Strategy: listen for attitude, interact naturally.

55
00:03:22.407 --> 00:03:23.570
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:26.736
Frankly, I think the plan is too expensive.

57
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.068
I see your point, but I would prefer the park.

58
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:38.373
Read the questions first, notice the speaker's attitude and tone, and in Speaking justify your ideas and respond to your partner.

59
00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:42.907
Be careful! Don't say: I only answer yes or no.

60
00:03:44.867 --> 00:03:47.400
Say: I justify and respond.

61
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.317
Interact with your partner.

62
00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.797
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.135
Listening and Speaking.

64
00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:58.572
Kunthea listens to a short interview with an architect.

65
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.983
The architect says frankly that the project is too expensive.

66
00:04:03.967 --> 00:04:06.338
She notices the worried tone of the voice.

67
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:11.063
In Speaking she compares two photos and justifies her choice.

68
00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:14.159
She asks her partner for his opinion.

69
00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:19.408
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.120
B2 First Listening has blank parts.

71
00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.482
A, four. B, two. C, nine.

72
00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.812
The answer is A: four.

73
00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.822
The speaker said the project is blank.

74
00:04:35.122 --> 00:04:39.170
A, finished. B, too expensive. C, cheap.

75
00:04:42.733 --> 00:04:45.244
The answer is B: too expensive.

76
00:04:46.383 --> 00:04:48.917
In Speaking Part 2 you blank two photos.

77
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:52.685
A, draw. B, delete. C, compare.

78
00:04:56.233 --> 00:04:58.059
The answer is C: compare.

79
00:04:59.217 --> 00:05:00.821
To justify is to blank.

80
00:05:01.121 --> 00:05:05.181
A, give reasons. B, ignore. C, guess.

81
00:05:08.733 --> 00:05:10.826
The answer is A: give reasons.

82
00:05:11.983 --> 00:05:13.948
What helps you hear attitude?

83
00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:18.041
A, a clock. B, tone of voice. C, a map.

84
00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.809
The answer is B: tone of voice.

85
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.221
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:32.557
How do you prepare for Listening and Speaking in B2 First?

87
00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.071
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:43.371 --> 00:05:58.437
I read the questions before I listen and then notice the speaker's attitude and tone. In Speaking I justify my choices with reasons, ask my partner questions and respond to their ideas. I practise both skills every week.

89
00:05:58.737 --> 00:06:00.423
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:01.317 --> 00:06:07.452
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: listen for attitude, interact naturally.

91
00:06:07.752 --> 00:06:12.204
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:15.354
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:15.654 --> 00:06:18.387
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

